# Consumer data-attribute surface sync

Editing preflight `data-*` (or the skill map for them)? **Same change** update every surface — no “docs later”.

## Required same-change set

1. Effect CSS under `packages/react/src/core/preflight/` (+ `preflight.css` import if new module)
2. `packages/react/src/core/specs/attributes.xml` (+ related core units when relevant)
3. `skills/viraui-design/custom-attributes.md` (when/how map) — **always** for consumer-facing add/change/remove
4. `skills/viraui-setup/preflight.md` when bootstrap/attr tables change

## Link chrome (`data-no-link-style`)

- Preflight styles every `a:any-link` unless `data-no-link-style` is present.
- Class presence does **not** opt out. Do not reintroduce `:not([class])` heuristics in skill copy.
- Prose links keep styles; chrome links set the attr (`ButtonLink`, `Chip`, `Menu.LinkItem`, custom Surface-as-a).

## Before done

Diff preflight `[data-*]` selectors vs `core/specs/attributes.xml` + `custom-attributes.md`. No stale rows.
